This change includes:
* an entire preprocessing pipeline for the WESAD data;

* a LSTM model which is capable of predicting, based on WESAD data, if a person is stressed or not;

* notebooks to overview the the data, the processing and the training of the model;

* conversion of the tf model to tf lite, so it would be able to run on phone.

On mobile, the virtual keyboard stays visible while scrolling search results in Command Universe, Command Library, and Customize Toolbar — obstructing results on small screens.

## Changes

- **`SearchCommands.tsx`**: Adds a capture-phase `scroll` listener that blurs the search input on scroll, dismissing the virtual keyboard. Guarded by `isTouch` so desktop is unaffected. Follows the same pattern used by `SortButton` to close its dropdown on scroll.

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!isTouch) return
  /** Blurs the input to dismiss the virtual keyboard. */
  const handleScroll = () => {
    inputRef.current?.blur()
  }
  window.addEventListener('scroll', handleScroll, true)
  return () => {
    window.removeEventListener('scroll', handleScroll, true)
  }
}, [])
```
